TITLE:: PipeWire
SUMMARY:: Utilities for working with PipeWire.
CATEGORIES:: Core

DESCRIPTION::
A set of utilities for working with PipeWire. MIDI keyboards are subscribed to the MIDI interface with CODE::aconnect::.

CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: connectToSoundcard
Connects the specified hardware synthesizer to the soundcard.

This is done by reading the LINK::Classes/Synthesizer#-inputBusChannels:: property and connecting those port numbers in PipeWire. If a link cannot be made, a warning is posted.

The logic for making the connections is as follows:

TABLE::
    ## Number of input bus channels || Behaviour ||
    ## 0 || Nothing is done. ||
    ## 1 || The synthesizer's input is connected to both the left and the right output channels of the soundcard. ||
    ## 2 || The synthesizer's first input is connected to left output channel of the soundcard and the second input is connected to the right channel. ||
    ## More than 2 || Nothing is connected, and a warning is posted. ||
::

ARGUMENT:: synthesizer
An instance of LINK::Classes/Synthesizer:: or LINK::Classes/HardwareSynthesizerConfig::.

METHOD:: connectAllToSoundcard
Calls LINK::Classes/PipeWire#*connectToSoundcard:: for each hardware synthesizer configured in LINK::Classes/Config#*hardwareSynthesizers::.

METHOD:: disconnectFromSoundcard
Disconnects the specified hardware synthesizer from the soundcard.

This is done by reading the LINK::Classes/Synthesizer#-inputBusChannels:: property and disconnecting those port numbers in PipeWire.

NOTE::
After running this method, you will not hear any sound from this particular hardware synthesizer unless:
LIST::
## the LINK::Classes/Server:: is running
## you run a SynthDef to capture its input.
::
You may wish to use the Synths page in LINK::Classes/SequencerGui:: to help with this.
::

ARGUMENT:: synthesizer
An instance of LINK::Classes/Synthesizer:: or LINK::Classes/HardwareSynthesizerConfig::.

METHOD:: disconnectAllFromSoundcard
Calls LINK::Classes/PipeWire#*disconnectFromSoundcard:: for each hardware synthesizer configured in LINK::Classes/Config#*hardwareSynthesizers::.

NOTE::
After running this method, you will not hear any sound from the hardware synthesizers unless:
LIST::
## the LINK::Classes/Server:: is running
## you run some SynthDefs to capture their input.
::
You may wish to use the Synths page in LINK::Classes/SequencerGui:: to help with this.
::

METHOD:: connectMidiKeyboards
Subscribes each keyboard in LINK::Classes/Config#*midiKeyboards:: to ALSA port CODE::0:: of the device name in LINK::Classes/Config#*midi::. The command is CODE::aconnect::, using the keyboard's client name and port index.

A keyboard that is not plugged in is skipped. A subscription that already exists is left in place. Any other failure posts a warning.

METHOD:: disconnectMidiKeyboards
Removes the subscriptions made by LINK::#*connectMidiKeyboards::. A keyboard that is not plugged in, or that was not subscribed, is skipped.

PRIVATE:: prAconnect, prLink, prUnlink
